<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Pu Luong by Motorbike: Luggage Packing Guide</h1>
<p>Packing for the Pu Luong ride is a negotiation between what the rider wants to carry and what the chain wants to carry for them, and the chain does not negotiate. The corridor out of Hanoi keeps things simple with heat and traffic, the karst legs complicate them with curves that interrogate every strap, and the valley settles the argument with damp air, mist and surfaces that answer to the last shower. Luggage done well disappears into the ride; luggage done badly joins the ride, leaning into corners and arguing with the brakes. This guide arranges weight, rain protection and priorities for the chain without inventing a single condition.</p>
<p>The machine, the briefing and the fallback plans come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk debriefs every rider back from the southwest chain. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, study the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the machines and terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
<nav class="toc">
